  "answer": "I'll look through the storefront cart API and how store merchant configuration is read so the line-quantity limit can be enforced without a restart.The cart writes all go through one facade, and merchant config is already loaded from the database on each read. I\u2019ll enforce the line limit there, before anything is saved.The storefront cart API now rejects any create, add, or quantity change that would leave a line with more units than the store allows. The limit is the merchant configuration `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY`, read from the database on each request so a change applies without a restart, and it defaults to 99 when that setting is missing. A quantity of 0 still removes the line. Requests over the limit return HTTP 400 and the cart is not saved.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses from the cart endpoints\", \"that the cart is unchanged after a rejected quantity\", \"that a CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY change applies without a restart\"], \"missing\": [\"a runnable cart API test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and posts a line over that limit\"]}",
